.TH hsh 1 "May 2026" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
hsh \- a simple UNIX command interpreter written in C

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple shell created as part of the Holberton School curriculum.

This project was built to help us better understand how a UNIX shell
works internally by recreating some of the basic behaviors of
the standard shell.

The shell reads commands from standard input, interprets them,
creates child processes, and executes programs using
the
.B execve
system call.

It supports both interactive and non-interactive execution modes.

.SH HOW IT WORKS
The shell performs the following steps:

.TP
1.
Displays a prompt and waits for user input

.TP
2.
Reads the command entered by the user

.TP
3.
Parses the command and its arguments

.TP
4.
Creates a child process using
.B fork

.TP
5.
Executes the command using
.B execve

.TP
6.
Waits for the child process to finish before displaying the prompt again

.SH FEATURES
.TP
Execute commands with arguments
.TP
Handle commands using the PATH environment variable
.TP
Interactive mode support
.TP
Non-interactive mode support
.TP
EOF handling using Ctrl + D

.SH USAGE
Interactive mode:

.B
./hsh

Example:

.B
($) /bin/ls

Non-interactive mode:

.B
echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh

.SH RETURN VALUE
The shell returns 0 on success or exits when an error or EOF is encountered.

